# STE-6 — copy to `be/.env` (gitignored) and fill in what you need.
#
# Nothing here is required to run the API: every address defaults to what
# docs/deployments.md records, and the network defaults to testnet. Set a value
# only to point somewhere else.

# --- server -----------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3001
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- network ----------------------------------------------------------------
# STELLAR_NETWORK=testnet
# STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE="Test SDF Network ; September 2015"
# STELLAR_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# STELLAR_HORIZON_URL=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org
# STELLAR_FRIENDBOT_URL=https://friendbot.stellar.org

# --- addresses (default: parsed from docs/deployments.md) -------------------
# SUSD_ISSUER=
# SUSD_DISTRIBUTOR=
# SUSD_SAC=
# EVENT_REGISTRY=
# RACE_RECORD=

# --- database (STE-11 PII vault) --------------------------------------------
# Local Postgres from compose.yaml at the repo root: `docker compose up -d postgres`.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://sterun:sterun@127.0.0.1:55432/sterun

# --- PII encryption (STE-11) -------------------------------------------------
# The vault refuses to start without a key rather than storing PII in the clear.
# Keys are numbered so they can be rotated without a synchronous re-encrypt:
# add a new one, move PII_ACTIVE_KEY_ID to it, let the old rows catch up.
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log('1:'+require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Custody, rotation and breach scope: be/OPERATIONS.md
# PII_KEYS=1:<64 hex>
# PII_ACTIVE_KEY_ID=1

# --- faucet -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed ONLY to pay out sUSD (`pnpm faucet` without --no-payout). The API
# server never needs it. This key can move the entire test supply: keep it in
# be/.env, which is gitignored, and never anywhere else in the repo.
# SUSD_DISTRIBUTOR_SECRET=

# Stroops per claim. 500000000 = 50 sUSD (10 paid entries at the 5 sUSD fee).
# FAUCET_AMOUNT_STROOPS=500000000

# --- indexer + TTL keeper (STE-16) -------------------------------------------
# The poller and the keeper are separate processes from the API:
#   pnpm indexer follow    getEvents -> Postgres
#   pnpm keeper run        pay rent on race records (weekly cron)
# Both need DATABASE_URL. Everything below has a working default.

# Any account that EXISTS on the network. It signs nothing and pays nothing:
# view calls are simulated, and a simulation still needs a source account to
# build an envelope around. Defaults to the sUSD distributor.
# INDEXER_SOURCE_ACCOUNT=

# 5-10s is the ticket's recommendation; 7s sits in the middle of it.
# INDEXER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=7000
# INDEXER_PAGE_LIMIT=200

# Where a first-ever poll starts. Unset means "as far back as RPC still
# retains", which is the most complete answer available.
# INDEXER_START_LEDGER=

# Pays for ExtendFootprintTTLOp. Needs XLM and nothing else — extending a TTL
# requires no authorization from anybody, so this key controls no records and
# can spend nothing but its own fees. `pnpm keeper scan` needs no key at all.
# TTL_KEEPER_SECRET=

# Ledgers, ~5s each. The threshold matches the contract's own BUMP_THRESHOLD
# (~120 days). The extend target is ONE LEDGER BELOW max_entry_ttl, and the -1
# is deliberate: ExtendFootprintTTLOp rejects the boundary as malformed, while
# the contract's own extend_ttl clamps to it. See be/src/keeper/ttl.ts.
# TTL_THRESHOLD_LEDGERS=2073600
# TTL_EXTEND_TO_LEDGERS=3110399
